-- title:
--   Initial and phase-zero auxiliary numerical profiles
-- statement:
--   Literal arrays store the phase-zero output promotion table $P_0(a,n)$ and joint table $J_0(w,a,n)$, with offsets $12a+n$ and $144w+12a+n$. The initial numerical bounds combine the initial profile ray with
--   $$
--   P_{\rm initial}(a,n)=C_{\rm ray}(a+1,n),\qquad
--   J_{\rm initial}(w,a,n)=M_{\rm ray}(w,a)+C_{\rm ray}(a+1,n).
--   $$
--   The next numerical bounds combine the first profile image with the two stored output tables. Out-of-range array reads use the specified zero default.
-- source:
--   Formalization for https://prove2.me/campaigns/block-sensitivity-vs-sensitivity; task source lean/Solutions/LocalNumericData.lean lines 8–839; SHA256 bc79d6b631e34b7aa5828bc5675fa255ce032e99abf9024db2c28eafe295ffa3; original campaign checkpoint SHA256 ed463039fb45e15e0e62a99e149dc811ac44ae8f790a5ae03ea5a7501f0639df.

